# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
#
# **Root-anchored on purpose.** These come from GitHub's Python template, where they are
# sdist/wheel build output at the top level. Unanchored they match a directory of that name at
# any depth, and the frontend under `ui/` has a real, tracked `ui/lib/` (19 files: the API
# client, the zod contract, the stream mapper). An unanchored `lib/` silently excluded the whole
# thing when the two repositories merged — `git status` clean, nothing to add, no error anywhere.
# `ui/build` and `ui/dist` are covered by ui/.gitignore's own entries below.
.Python
/build/
/develop-eggs/
/dist/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/
/share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
#   Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#   before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec

